{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459550-two-questions-about-high-humanity-vampires","id":1459550,"title":"Two questions about high - humanity vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-10T06:41:32-07:00","id":1459550,"title":"Two questions about high - humanity vampires","content":"First: if 16 th generation vampires ( described in Beckett's Journal ) can eat and even ( with effort ) digest normal food, grows hairs and nails, perspirate, breath, have heartbeat and are - supposedly - able to conceive...<br /> <br /> and, if according to the rules about the Blush of Life, vampires with humanity 8 and higher can be constantly in this state, without spending Vitae...<br /> <br /> ...what would look like a Humanity 10, 16th generation vampire? <br /> <br /> <br /> Second: a vampire who never committed sins worth atoning ( starts as high Mortality human, gets embraced by a mid-high Humanity kindred, choose seclusion and feeding on animal blood ) would find easier or harder to attain Golconda? Because he's innocent, but also ignorant ( never truly experienced what the Beast can do ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T07:30:45-07:00","id":1459554,"title":"","content":"Aren't 16th gens essentially Dhampir/Revenant territory rather than vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T07:37:45-07:00","id":1459556,"title":"","content":"Mhhh... no , they are undead. Barely, but undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T07:51:16-07:00","id":1459557,"title":"","content":"1) up to ST<br /> <br /> 2) fairly certain golconda is a personal journey that can't be thought or shown so they could by accident, they just wouldn't know what it's called","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T14:47:29-07:00","id":1459585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459550-two-questions-about-high-humanity-vampires?p=1459554#post1459554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't 16th gens essentially Dhampir/Revenant territory rather than vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> Basically V5 eliminated the hard end of the Curse. By the time you get to 14th gen Thin Blood your chances at Embracing are reduced, but if you get there the result is just as potent as you. So we already have 15th and 16th gens and they're mechanically identical and effectively the future of the Kindred. Hooray.<br /> <br /> A Humanity 10 16th gen vamp would be whatever the ST wants, but probably not a lot healthier. I would personally just use RAW and don't think a lot about this unless the character needs additional effects, which can be done through special merits or something.<br /> <br /> Golconda is a personal journey without much in terms of rules, but overall it is stated as hard for everyone, with some really weird exceptions. Personally I think such vampires would need to leave their bubbles and face challenges to their Humanity, at the very least, but otherwise wouldn't have necessarily a harder or easier time getting there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T16:40:04-07:00","id":1459597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459550-two-questions-about-high-humanity-vampires?p=1459554#post1459554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't 16th gens essentially Dhampir/Revenant territory rather than vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>In V20 a Dhampir and 16th Gen are very different.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs have a 10 point blood pool that can boost stats and heal at normal cost and while they can\u2019t feed on mortals, naturally regain 1 point per day. 16th Gens have only 4 they can spend on anything other than rising and pay double for anything but rising and since they can only spend 1/turn means it takes twice as long to activate any disciplines/heal etc. and have to refill after practically any use.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs are immune to sunlight. 16th Gens treat sunlight as lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs can eat and digest food. 16th Gens can only hold it down, but gain no nourishment from it and must regurgitate it eventually.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs treat treats agg as lethal (so can soak it with Stamina and heal it at 1 blood per health level), but takes full damage from bashing and can be killed by lethal damage. 16th Gens take half from bashing, but otherwise take damage and heal just like any other vampire.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs can learn only the first dot of any discipline and drinking vampire blood does NOT make them a ghoul (so they can\u2019t learn higher tiers like a ghoul with a low gen domitor can), but can bind them. 16th Gens can learn up to 2 dots in any disciplines.<br /> <br /> A Dhampir can\u2019t improve its \u201cgeneration\u201d and would only become a vampire if embraced. A 16th Gen has been embraced and so can improve its generation through diablerie.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs have a weaker Beast, they\u2019re immune to hunger and fear frenzy and have -2 difficulty to resist anger triggers and can never lose their last dot of humanity. 16th Gens suffer the full effects of Frenzy and can enter Wassail like any Kindred.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs age very slowly. 16th Gens are actually immortal.<br /> <br /> Basically V20 16th Gens are a step up, barely, from a standard ghoul or revenant and a clear step down from 15th Gens. Dhampirs in V20 get a degree of hybrid vigor (its a real thing with crossbred species) and are in several ways stronger than their 15-16th Gen parent... mainly via traits that could be better described as \u201caugmented mortal\u201d than \u201cweak vampire.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T23:21:17-07:00","id":1459822,"title":"","content":"V20 core has rules up to 15th gen and no rules at all for Dhampirs. Revenants &amp; Ghouls has nothing on them either, but it (and the core) has changed rules on Revenants dropping their bloodpool from 10 to 2 so why wouldn\u2019t the same be true of Dhampirs?<br /> <br /> Or does Becket\u2019s Journal give them a full 10 point pool? Can\u2019t remember but considering their rules have always mirrored the Revenants it would be odd for them to have 10 point pool of usable Blood. Especially since even the Generations loose Blood pool 16th at 4 it would be reasonable to assume Dhampirs would have the pool at 2, reducing it by 2 points per generation beyond 13th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":". 09-13-2021, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T00:05:56-07:00","id":1459824,"title":"","content":"Checked Becketts...<br /> <br /> They do have a pool of 10 Blood... I wonder if the writer knew of the changes to Revenants though. Like said they used to mirror each other on most rules but this is a huge disparity here. A difference of 8 points in Blood pool sizes is ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T03:15:37-07:00","id":1459831,"title":"","content":"This is a really cool debate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T08:35:07-07:00","id":1459850,"title":"","content":"I always took the notion that Dhampirs and Revenants were identical to be mostly in-universe attributions from guys like Netchurch who really want to pretend \u201cscience\u201d can explain the vampire condition. But even back in Revised, revenants burned blood volume just like ghouls and vampires, while right from the start dhampirs\u2019 pool was entirely a spiritual charge to their blood.<br /> <br /> The BJD updates just make it clearer that there is a difference between the inbreeding of ghouls and the hybrid vigor (outbreeding) of a dhampir. Most notably isn\u2019t even the size of the blood pool, but that dhampirs are more physically resilient than revenants (they treat all aggravated damage as lethal and have a much easier check for regrowing lost limbs), do not suffer fear or hunger frenzies and no matter how much vitae they consume cannot become ghouls (I give them the vampire price for unbondable for this reason). It doesn\u2019t take much in the way of merits to turn them into what I\u2019ve presented them as in my campaign; spiritual antibodies against the Curse of Caine.<br /> <br /> I honestly prefer that there are differences precisely because inbreeding plus blood magic shouldn\u2019t produce identical results to a natural unforced endpoint to the Curse of Caine. There\u2019s more story potential in dhampirs as something new and different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T10:39:46-07:00","id":1459864,"title":"","content":"I kinda thought the idea that they'd be different is some 90's/Early 2000's sillyness. VTM doesn't want to be Blade or underworld. Crazy super hybrids aren't it's thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T11:13:07-07:00","id":1459867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459550-two-questions-about-high-humanity-vampires?p=1459864#post1459864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda thought the idea that they'd be different is some 90's/Early 2000's sillyness. VTM doesn't want to be Blade or underworld. Crazy super hybrids aren't it's thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>What super-hybrids are you seeing?<br /> <br /> They're stronger than a ghoul or revenant, but still fall well behind even a 13th Gen vampire and their only real edge in actual play is being quite resilient to aggravated damage (walking in sunlight by contrast is a nothing burger in actual play since you've got other players at the table who the ST isn't going to sideline for long... so your days just get FF'd through so everyone can get back to participating).<br /> <br /> Likewise, their ability to improve is exceedingly limited. Since they can't become a ghoul they can't learn any discipline past the first dot ever (no stint with a low gen vamp or the alternate Ghouls &amp; Revenants table to get around it either). We've got one Revenant in the game who ghouled to an 8th Gen and (using the alternate Ghouls &amp; Revenants rules) just picked up their 3rd dot in one of their disciplines. No Dhampir as written can possibly do that. They get other benefits instead.<br /> <br /> So its not Blade, its just not &quot;the gimp show.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}